<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">First Hellenic Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1822 CE – 1832 CE · capital Nauplia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The provisional Greek state of the War of Independence, from the constitution of Epidaurus in 1822 to the arrival of a king in 1832.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In January 1822 the First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/epidaurus">Epidaurus</a> declared Greek independence and adopted a provisional constitution, uniting the regional governments such as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peloponnesian-senate">Peloponnesian Senate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandros-mavrokordatos">Alexandros Mavrokordatos</a> was elected president of the executive. The new state controlled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, parts of the mainland and many islands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Divided between notables, islanders and military chiefs, the government fell into civil war in 1823-1825 just as Ibrahim Pasha's Egyptian army invaded. The intervention of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-navarino">Navarino</a> in 1827 saved the revolution. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannis-kapodistrias">Ioannis Kapodistrias</a>, elected governor, arrived in 1828 and built a central administration at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a>, founding schools and a currency, the phoenix.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-protocol-1830">London Protocol</a> of 1830 recognised Greek independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannis-kapodistrias">Kapodistrias</a> was assassinated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a> in October 1831, and chaos followed. In 1832 the great powers chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-of-greece">Otto of Bavaria</a> as king, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece">Kingdom of Greece</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/first-hellenic-republic.jpg" alt="First Hellenic Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: (of code) Makaristos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Greece_(1822-1978).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1822 CE – 1832 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nauplia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alexandros Mavrokordatos, Ioannis Kapodistrias, Augustinos Kapodistrias</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Provisional Administration of Greece, Hellenic State (1828-1832)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1827&amp;focus=first-hellenic-republic" aria-label="First Hellenic Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5250 826 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where First Hellenic Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5570 1082L5562 1111M5570 1082L5556 1051M5570 1082L5533 1056M5570 1082L5709 970M5570 1082L5591 1068"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5562 1111h0M5556 1051h0M5533 1056h0M5709 970h0M5591 1068h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5570 1082h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5570 1082h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1827&amp;focus=first-hellenic-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
